{"name":"Wedding Dress","hex":"#fefee7","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wedding dress","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The dress worn by a bride during a wedding ceremony, traditionally white with a long train in Western culture."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wedding_dress"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wedding dress","blocks":[{"text":"A wedding dress or bridal gown is the dress worn by the bride during a wedding ceremony."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/41/Weddingdress2024.jpg/330px-Weddingdress2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wedding_dress","wikidata":"Q170063"},{"title":"Wedding Dress (Taeyang song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Wedding Dress\" is a song recorded by South Korean singer Taeyang, and released as the second single of his first studio album Solar (2010) on November 13, 2009, through YG Entertainment. It was written by Teddy Park and composed by Park and Taeyang."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8e/Wedding_Dress_Taeyang.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wedding_Dress_(Taeyang_song)","wikidata":"Q16167374"},{"title":"Wedding","blocks":[{"text":"A wedding is a ceremony in which two people are united in marriage. Wedding traditions and customs vary greatly between cultures, ethnicities, races, religions, denominations, countries, social classes, and sexual orientations. Most wedding ceremonies involve an exchange of marriage vows by a couple; a presentation of a gift ; and a public proclamation of marriage by an authority figure or celebrant. Special wedding garments are often worn, and the ceremony is sometimes followed by a wedding reception. Music, poetry, prayers, or readings from religious texts or literature are also commonly incorporated into the ceremony, as well as superstitious customs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Hindu_wedding_rituals_b_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Hindu_wedding_rituals_b_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wedding","wikidata":"Q49836"},{"title":"Dress","blocks":[{"text":"A dress is a one-piece outer garment that is worn on the torso, hanging down over the legs. Dresses often consist of a bodice attached to a skirt."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Afternoon_ensemble_MET_63.212a-b_CP4.jpg/330px-Afternoon_ensemble_MET_63.212a-b_CP4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dress","wikidata":"Q200539"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/1840_blue_wedding_dress.jpg/500px-1840_blue_wedding_dress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/1840_blue_wedding_dress.jpg/1280px-1840_blue_wedding_dress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/1840_blue_wedding_dress.jpg/500px-1840_blue_wedding_dress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A blue wedding dress from 1840","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1840_blue_wedding_dress.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Bologna_marriage_women.jpg/120px-Bologna_marriage_women.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/95/Bologna_marriage_women.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Bologna_marriage_women.jpg/120px-Bologna_marriage_women.jpg?utm_source=en.wikip